The video is not.

    green-screen-trex.mp4

    Downloaded from Pixabay. By Exceptional_3D, under the Pixabay Content License.

      source:  https://pixabay.com/videos/dinosaur-trex-reptile-roar-extinct-170831/
      licence: https://pixabay.com/service/license-summary/

The Pixabay Content License grants free commercial and non-commercial use and requires no
attribution. The attribution above is given anyway, because a reader of this repository
needs to know the file did not come from here -- the maintainer can neither place it
under MIT nor reserve rights over it.

It is committed as the forcing case ADR-0088 measures its keyer against: 1920x1080, h264,
24 fps, 140 frames. chroma_key_scan.sh beside it re-derives every number in that ADR from
this file and exits non-zero the moment one stops reproducing.


One question this file does not settle
--------------------------------------

The clip is committed verbatim as downloaded -- no trim, no edit. The Pixabay terms
forbid distributing Content "on a Standalone basis", defined as "where no creative effort
has been applied to the Content and it remains in substantially the same form as it
exists on the Service". Every example those terms give of the prohibition is a resale:
prints, wallpapers, posters, NFTs, merchandise. A test fixture inside a source repository
is plainly not one of those -- and it is equally plainly an unedited copy being
redistributed.

The question is open, it is tracked as its own issue, and nothing here resolves it.
